In this laboratory activity, I learned the basic structure and syntax of XML by creating a simple student data document. I learned that XML must have a single root element, properly nested elements, and matching opening and closing tags. I also validated my XML document to check if there were any syntax errors. The validation process helped me understand the importance of following the correct XML structure. Overall, this activity gave me a better understanding of how XML can organize and store data in a format that can be easily shared and used by different systems.

